// A FLOAT field carrying a bracketed RANGE in a machine's attached data makes
// the machine unplannable. One token decides it, and neither float-ness nor
// range-ness alone is enough:
//
//   value: i32                checks
//   value: f32                checks
//   value: i32 [0..=10]       checks   <- an integer range is fine
//   value: f64 in Finite      checks   <- a float DOMAIN is fine
//   value: f32 [0.0..=1.0]    OMITTED  (this fixture)
//   value: f64 [0.0..=1.0]    OMITTED
//
// all at `state graph: state signature: parameter signature: attached data
// shape`.
//
// The phase name misleads on "parameter signature": a state parameter is not
// required, and the same program with a parameterless state omits
// identically.
//
// THE DECLINING EXIT IS CONFIRMED, not guessed. The mark sits above four `?`
// exits in `terminal_unit/calls/signatures.rs`. Marking each distinctly and
// counting them on the failing and the working program: attached-name,
// data-definition and `scalar_and_structural_parameters` decline the same
// number of times in both (1654, 118, 68), while
// `shapes.add_attached_application` declines 23 times against 19. That
// difference of four is the entire gap.
//
// From there the chain is `add_attached_application` -> `add_attached_data`
// -> `add_data_shape` in `terminal_unit/types/mod.rs`, which walks the
// data's fields. That walk is where a bracketed range on a float field has
// to become representable. The file is held by LOCAL-DATA-CLUSTER-REPAIR.
//
// FOUR of the five corpus fixtures at this phase carry a float-range field:
// `pass/float/finite_core_domain_range_discharge`,
// `pass/recast/runtime_float_range_representation_recast_exit`,
// `pass/recast/runtime_mutable_equivalent_record_recast_exit` and
// `pass/recast/runtime_shared_record_float_range_weakening_exit` -- the last
// two carry theirs inside a record, so the shell does not have to be the
// attached type's own field list. The fifth,
// `pass/generics/runtime_const_container_methods_exit`, has no float at all
// (its attached fields are `FixedBuffer<2>` and `FixedBuffer<4>`) and is a
// DIFFERENT cause, unattributed.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    value: f32 [0.0..=1.0];
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    transition { _ -> step(1) }

    state step(&mut self, count: i32) {
        self.console.exit_process(0);
    }
}
